                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4c0380ff-6ac2-37df-a968-2b9499727068",
                        "entry_id": "d4121cef-e3ba-3e68-b00f-da470a312674",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The oesophagus; the gullet."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dialectal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6056a725-11f9-475e-b3aa-9bb3475f080c",
                                "sense_id": "4c0380ff-6ac2-37df-a968-2b9499727068",
                                "text": "By Heaven, and all saints in it, better food hath not passed my weasand for three livelong days, and by God’s providence it is that I am now here to tell it."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "768e5b72-c02f-3ff9-b210-775dff8ee0a6",
                        "entry_id": "d4121cef-e3ba-3e68-b00f-da470a312674",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The throat or windpipe."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dialectal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "17f86e9a-1afd-4cf5-ae8b-84f8a3efc9de",
                                "sense_id": "768e5b72-c02f-3ff9-b210-775dff8ee0a6",
                                "text": "[…] Or cut his vvezand vvith thy knife."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8804ab7c-f52b-4888-b384-099f5dd8a982",
                                "sense_id": "768e5b72-c02f-3ff9-b210-775dff8ee0a6",
                                "text": "[A]lthough the vveazon, throtle and tongue [of birds] be the inſtruments of voice, and by their agitations doe chiefly concurre unto theſe delightfull modulations, yet cannot vve aſſigne the cauſe unto any particular formation; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ec4db4c-e558-499c-ba3d-cb958ce1459a",
                                "sense_id": "768e5b72-c02f-3ff9-b210-775dff8ee0a6",
                                "text": "For at the Throat there are tvvo cavities or conducting parts: the one the Oeſophagus or Gullet, ſeated next the ſpine, a part official unto nutrition, and vvhereby the aliment both vvet and dry is conveied unto the ſtomack; the other (by vvhich tis conceived the Drink doth paſs) is the vveazon, rough artery, or vvind-pipe, a part inſervient to voice and reſpiration; for thereby the air deſcendeth into the lungs, and is communicated unto the heart […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "365f7518-f25c-4d49-b855-63b388d3a1b2",
                                "sense_id": "768e5b72-c02f-3ff9-b210-775dff8ee0a6",
                                "text": "Rat. / I’ll slily seize and / Let blood from her weasand,— / Creeping through crevice, and chink, and cranny, / With my snaky tail, and my sides so scranny."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8420e05c-15e3-4e7b-aca3-b5e112d6421e",
                                "sense_id": "768e5b72-c02f-3ff9-b210-775dff8ee0a6",
                                "text": "They're both so engrossed in this that they don't notice my landlady, who comes rushing out to learn what's going on. / \"Why,\" her son explains, \"he grabbed me by the weasand, it took me a long time to get my wind back.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "22879da8-68f0-4607-9c44-6d922e9ecda7",
                                "sense_id": "768e5b72-c02f-3ff9-b210-775dff8ee0a6",
                                "text": "‘Which fellows?’ Very loud now, but a tightening in her weasand."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
